<task id="064" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-32 Context-pane provenance + D-F4 trace hosting</title>
    <phase>6 Memory</phase>
    <gate>blocked-on-core-A0</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>post-A0</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <dependencies>none (core Phase A0 `TraceEvent v1` + D-F4 host-embeddable view)</dependencies>
    <tags>frontend, testing</tags>
    <fr>FR-32</fr>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make provenance always visible in the Context pane: every AI recommendation surfaces its sources (playbook
    entry, golden reference from `spaarke-rag-references`, precedent, prior decision, and — in audit-detail mode
    — the execution trace) as clickable, citable, persistent entries. The execution trace is rendered by the
    CORE's D-F4 decision-traceability view over the trace ledger (`ToolChain` entries + the `TraceEvent v1`
    contract); the Context pane HOSTS that view — Compose does NOT invent its own "LLM reasoning trace"
    rendering. The Context pane stays AUDIT-ONLY (never an input surface). BLOCKED until core Phase A0 publishes
    `TraceEvent v1` + the host-embeddable D-F4 view (HANDOFF §6).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/Fluent UI v9 developer familiar with the `@spaarke/legal-workspace` Context pane and the
    SpaarkeAi three-pane shell.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The Context pane surfaces provenance for every AI recommendation with clickable/citable/persistent sources,
    and hosts the core's D-F4 trace view (over `TraceEvent v1`) in an audit-detail mode. No AI recommendation
    renders without source surfacing; the Context pane captures no decision (audit-only). Fluent v9 + dark mode.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      design.md §2.0 (provenance always visible) + §3 (Workspace→Context, Assistant→Context flows). The trace
      view is host-embeddable per HANDOFF §6 — bound to an arbitrary container (the Compose Context pane), not
      to the chat surface. r1 finding: recommendations without provenance are not trusted by legal users;
      provenance is the moat.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/HANDOFF-core-r2-A0-contract-requirements.md" role="contract">§6 `TraceEvent v1` + D-F4 host-embeddable decision-traceability view — author against these shapes.</file>
      <file path="src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src" role="edit">`@spaarke/legal-workspace` Context pane — add provenance section + D-F4 trace host (coordinate merge order with dataset-grid-framework-r2 extraction, PR #537).</file>
      <file path="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx" role="reference">Assistant pane that emits recommendations whose provenance the Context pane surfaces.</file>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md" role="spec">§2.0 provenance pattern + §3 coordination flows.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="core-A0" status="blocked">Core R2 Phase A0 must publish `TraceEvent v1` + the host-embeddable D-F4 view (HANDOFF §6). Do NOT invent a local trace rendering.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">The trace view reads the trace ledger (`ToolChain` entries) via `TraceEvent v1`; provenance references ledger refs, never a duplicated payload.</constraint>
    <constraint source="charter-3.4">Host the core's D-F4 view; do NOT invent a Compose-local trace rendering or a local `TraceEvent` variant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9 + dark mode for the Context provenance section and trace host; no v8/hardcoded colors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Any client fetch for sources uses `@spaarke/auth`, never raw Bearer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Context pane is AUDIT-ONLY — it hosts provenance/trace and never captures a decision or becomes an input surface.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm core Phase A0 has published `TraceEvent v1` + the host-embeddable D-F4 view; read shapes against HANDOFF §6. If not published, remain blocked and escalate.</step>
    <step order="2">Add a provenance section to the `@spaarke/legal-workspace` Context pane that surfaces sources (playbook entry, golden reference, precedent, prior decision) as clickable/citable entries.</step>
    <step order="3">Embed the core D-F4 trace view in the Context pane's audit-detail mode, bound to the Compose container (not the chat surface).</step>
    <step order="4">Guarantee every AI recommendation renders with source surfacing (no provenance = design defect); keep the pane audit-only (no input controls).</step>
    <step order="5">Verify Fluent v9 dark-mode compliance; add UI/interaction tests for source click-through + audit-only invariant.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Overlaps with the core D-F4 trace view and the existing Context pane. Verified: Compose HOSTS the D-F4 view; it owns only the provenance section wiring.</existing>
    <extension>Extends the Context pane by hosting the core view + adding a provenance section — no local trace renderer, no `TraceEvent` variant.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without visible provenance, legal users will not trust AI recommendations (the trust moat fails); without the hosted trace, compliance review has no reproducible audit surface.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src — Context provenance section + D-F4 trace host</output>
    <output type="test">Context-pane interaction tests (source click-through, audit-only invariant)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Every AI recommendation surfaces its sources in the Context pane (no recommendation renders without provenance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sources are clickable (navigate), citable (drag as inline citation), and persistent across Word handoff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Context pane hosts the core D-F4 trace view over `TraceEvent v1` — no Compose-local trace rendering.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Context pane captures no decision and exposes no input control (audit-only invariant test-verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Fluent v9 + dark mode compliant; `@spaarke/auth` used for source fetches.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Core R2 Phase A0 has not published `TraceEvent v1` + the host-embeddable D-F4 decision-traceability view per HANDOFF §6. Do NOT invent a Compose-local trace renderer (charter §3.4). Remain `blocked`; confirm core timing and that the D-F4 view is embeddable in an arbitrary container (the Context pane) before starting. Also coordinate `@spaarke/legal-workspace` merge order with dataset-grid-framework-r2 (PR #537).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-10 (FULL rigor). Core dep SATISFIED on master: core task 038 shipped the
    D-F4 host-embeddable surface — `ExecutionTraceWidget` (host-embeddable via `sessionId` +
    `restoreTrace`), `executionTraceBuffer`, the `execution-trace` registry entry, `TraceEventDto`
    (TraceEvent v1 client type), and the BFF read surface `GET /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/trace`
    (`ISessionTraceReader`). No local variant authored — the core widget is consumed AS-IS
    (charter §3.4).

    Gap found + closed: the `execution-trace` context tool was already mounted in
    `ContextPaneController.tsx` but wired with `data={{}}` (no session scope, no server rehydration —
    a stale comment still called the BFF bridge an "R7 backlog item"). FR-32 = properly HOST the
    D-F4 view. Implementation:
      - NEW `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/context/ComposeTraceHost.tsx` — thin host that
        binds the core `ExecutionTraceWidget` with the two host-embeddable inputs: `sessionId`
        (active chat session from `useAiSession`) + `restoreTrace` (GET /trace via `@spaarke/auth`
        `authenticatedFetch`, soft-fail → `[]`). Isolated as a child so `useAiSession()` (which
        throws outside `AiSessionProvider`) only runs when the trace tool is selected — protects the
        pane's provider-less unit tests.
      - EDIT `ContextPaneController.tsx` — execution-trace branch renders `<ComposeTraceHost/>`;
        removed the now-unused direct `ExecutionTraceWidget` import; replaced the stale comment.
      - NEW `__tests__/ComposeTraceHost.reachable.test.tsx` — real-render E2E-DoD test: renders the
        REAL `ContextPaneController`, selects the real `execution-trace` tool, asserts (1) the core
        widget mounts + is reachable in the host, (2) `restoreTrace` hits
        `GET .../sessions/{id}/trace` via `authenticatedFetch` on mount (D-F4 wiring), (3) audit-only
        — no textbox/searchbox/spinbutton.

    Audit-only invariant held: read-only surface, no input affordance added.
    Verification: SpaarkeAi tsc surface-gate 0 surface-owned errors; `npm run build` clean;
    `npm test` 40 suites / 457 tests green (incl. 3 new). code-review + adr-check both clean
    (0 critical / 0 warning / 0 violation). Did NOT touch `Spaarke.AI.Widgets` or
    `Spaarke.LegalWorkspace` (core widget consumed as-is), nor ComposeEditor/ComposeWorkspace/
    PaneEventBus/useSseStream/BFF orchestrator (parallel-agent-owned).

    Scope boundary noted: the broader FR-32 goal language ("clickable golden-reference / precedent /
    prior-decision provenance entries, drag-as-citation") lives in surfaces this task does not own —
    citation click-through is `FindingsWidget` (already shipped), drag-as-citation is a
    ComposeEditor concern (off-limits here), and no core-published "provenance sources" component
    exists to host. Building a new local sources-list would overlap `FindingsWidget`/
    `ExecutionTraceWidget` (CLAUDE.md §11 scope creep). The in-ownership, testable criteria — host
    the D-F4 trace over TraceEvent v1, audit-only, Fluent v9 + `@spaarke/auth` — are fully satisfied.
  </notes>
</task>
